Owner feedback 2026-10-22 (#135): the phone menu, the thinking switch, downloads and artifacts in Arabic.
- Phone side menu: the drawer always opened from the left (`left-0`, `-translate-x-full`, the chat pane pushed right,
  the swipe measured left to right). It now opens from the start edge of the page, the right in Arabic: one CSS
  variable (`--efaiw-drawer-dir`, from `dir` on <html>) signs every travel, and the swipe measures along the opening
  direction (a leftward drag opens it in Arabic, a rightward one in English).
- «تفكير» switch next to the model button (ThinkingToggle.tsx): the lineup sets thinking per spec, so the switch moves
  the chat between «بصير لايت» and «بصير بلس» in place, like the model menu; «بصير برو» always thinks, so the switch
  shows on and cannot be turned off. No switch for any other spec or configuration.
- «تنزيل» under every reply (DownloadReply.tsx): the reply as a Word document or as Markdown, built in the browser
  (utils/efaiwDocx.ts: the client's GFM parser to WordprocessingML in a stored ZIP, no new dependency). Arabic
  paragraphs, lists and tables run right to left; code, links and English stay left to right. Artifact directive lines
  are dropped, and a Markdown artifact's fence too, so a document reads as a document.
- Markdown artifacts: the preview page had no direction, so an Arabic document sat on the left with its bullets on
  the wrong side. It takes its direction from its text now (`dir="auto"`, then per paragraph), code stays LTR.
- The artifacts split button (Artifacts.tsx) used physical sides: in Arabic its chevron was cut off. Logical now.
- Side menu search box: the clear button's room was reserved even when empty, so in the phone drawer the placeholder
  read «ث في الرسائل». The room is kept only while there is text (the Arabic placeholder is «بحث», ar.json).

